@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 600px; margin: 20px auto; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h2 style="color: #4CAF50; border-bottom: 2px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 10px;">📜 Our Ironclad Privacy Policy (Spoiler Alert)</h2>

    <p>You know how most companies have a 12,000-word Privacy Policy that you "agree" to by breathing near a keyboard? Ours is much shorter:</p>

    <blockquote style="border-left: 5px solid #ffcc00; padding: 10px 20px; margin: 15px 0; background-color: #fff9e6;">
        <p style="font-style: italic; font-weight: bold;">We Know Everything. Move On.</p>
    </blockquote>

    <p>Seriously, we've already correlated your search history for <strong>"quiet quitting guide"</strong> with the time you submitted that "Totally Anonymous" grievance last year. We've got algorithms tracking your exact number of Slack emojis per day and the precise hour you start typing in ALL CAPS.</p>

    <p>So, when the <strong>"Anonymous" Work Survey</strong> pops up, feel free to be yourself! Because rest assured, we're not asking for your feedback; we're just checking to make sure your answers match the highly detailed, personalized profile we've already compiled for you. It's for <strong>data consistency</strong>!</p>
</div>
